	(text "U1 -IN SENSE RUN to R5 bottom pad - NOT a GND symbol at U1"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 93.98 90.17 0.0000)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "77e5cf43-b005-436b-aad1-18d341c7e64f")
	)
	(text_box "NOTE 1  U1 -IN IS A DEDICATED SENSE RUN, NOT A GROUND SYMBOL.  It is wired by the explicit wire below to R5's bottom pad - the attenuator string's\n        bottom node - and meets GND only there.  A divider passes a ground offset at UNITY while dividing the signal by K = 0.400, so 1 mV of\n        offset between the string bottom and the converter is 2.5 mV at the terminal: half the 25 degC budget.  Bound: -IN must stay within\n        -0.3 V to +0.5 V of U1's GND pin (ADS8326, absolute).  P7 keeps it a dedicated run - constraints.json corridor R5 -> U1, 3 mm.\nNOTE 2  The guard ring around /AIN_DIV and U3 +IN is P7 COPPER on /AIN_BUF (the buffer OUTPUT), never on /AIN_DIV itself.  No schematic element.\nNOTE 3  R7 + C2 + C8 are the ADS8326's own recommended rail entry (figs 44/45): R7 upstream of both caps, C2 the smaller and closest to the pin.\n        It isolates U1 ALONE - U2 and U3 stay on +3V3 upstream of R7.  No ferrite anywhere.\nNOTE 4  NO series resistor between U2 VOUT and C3 / U1 REF (recorded ruling): a SAR's reference current varies with input code, so a series R\n        becomes a code-dependent nonlinearity.  C5 >= 1 uF is MANDATORY - the ADR4520's 1-100 uF load-capacitance window is two-ended.\nNOTE 5  R1-R5 are FIVE EQUAL 200 k elements in ONE string tapped 3:2 (K = 0.400, Rtot 1.00 Mohm, tap Thevenin 240 kohm).  Do not collapse."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
